  "packageSize": 36647,
  "published": "1900-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "releaseNotes": "2.3.0 — ADDITIVE (BG-2356, audit B-08): OutboxBacklog, the age of the oldest unpublished outbox row per topic, kept by OutboxRelay and read by a readiness check (Brainograph.ServiceDefaults 4.10.0 AddOutboxBacklogReadiness). OutboxRelay takes an optional trailing OutboxBacklog constructor parameter and exposes it as Backlog; a relay built without one keeps its own. The age is computed when it is READ, so a stalled relay or an unreadable database keeps ageing the last picture. Register one OutboxBacklog singleton (the order against AddHostedService<OutboxRelay>() does not matter) to share it with the readiness check; with two relays in one service the picture is last-writer-wins. No change for a service that does nothing. 2.0.0 — MessagingProvider reduced to { Wolverine }; RabbitMQ is now a Wolverine transport, not a separate provider. Breaking: removes the MessagingProvider.RabbitMq enum member (a source/compile break for any code that referenced it by name or exhaustively matched the enum; no consumer in this repo did).",
